  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohd. Khalid Ansari vs State Of U.P. on 28 October, 2025 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc:188932 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 35322 of 2025 Mohd. Khalid Ansari .....Applicant(s) Versus State of U.P. .....Opposite Party(s) Counsel for Applicant(s) : Ashish Goyal Counsel for Opposite Party(s) : G.A. Court No. - 68 Mohd. Khalid Ansari vs State Of U.P. on 28 October, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/155115841/ 1 Hon'Ble Ashutosh Srivastava, J. Supplementary affidavit is taken on record.",
    "facts": "This bail application under Section 483 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 has been moved on behalf of accused-applicant, Mohd. Khalid Ansari, seeking enlargement on bail in Case Crime No. 384 of 2025, under Sections 274, 275, 280 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 and Section 59 and 63 Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006, Police Station Pipraich , District Gorakhpur.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant argued that the accused-applicant is innocent. He has been falsely implicated in this very case crime number and is languishing in jail since 27.5.2025. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that similarly circumstanced co-accused Mohd. Wahid has already been enlarged on bail by co-ordinate Bench of this Court on 4.9.2025 in Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. 37461 of 2025. He has four cases of criminal antecedent, which have sufficiently been explained and there is no likelihood of his fleeing from course of justice or tampering with evidence in case of release on bail. Hence, bail has been prayed for. Per contra learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for bail of the applicant, but could not dispute the aforesaid fact.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant argued that the accused-applicant is innocent. He has been falsely implicated in this very case crime number and is languishing in jail since 27.5.2025. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that similarly circumstanced co-accused Mohd. Wahid has already been enlarged on bail by co-ordinate Bench of this Court on 4.9.2025 in Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. 37461 of 2025. He has four cases of criminal antecedent, which have sufficiently been explained and there is no likelihood of his fleeing from course of justice or tampering with evidence in case of release on bail. Hence, bail has been prayed for. Per contra learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for bail of the applicant, but could not dispute the aforesaid fact.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
